      "writtenOn": "2020-09-11T08:53:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change is mixing two pieces of functionality - adding structs and merging nested sets. I think that they should be split out into two separate changes:\n1. Transform struct into a BpPropertySet.\n2. Merging BpPropertySets together.\n\nThe current solution mixes those together which makes both parts more complicated than necessary. The logic for merging has to handle both structs and BpPropertySet. By having them as separate changes you can simplify each piece.\n\nI think that they will each need some unit tests, i.e. ones that don\u0027t require parsing a whole .bp file such as the existing ones in bp_test.go.",
      "revId": "e5bf895264f4551430e9e33b4d738d80d75559ff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3e1ad99_7f5a184b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-15T01:43:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, I tried that first. Handling it in two stages adds code to construct a full bpPropertySet rather than just merging the struct fields, duplicates a bit of type testing logic, and doesn\u0027t help with the messy logic handling new/existing values in AddProperty.\n\nSplitting out the merging code helps, which I\u0027ve done now. I\u0027ve also cleaned up some unnecessary complications trying to avoid adding empty sets.\n\nI\u0027ve split off the sanitizer and updater changes from the bp.go stuff and added unit tests, but there\u0027s not much value in separating out the property struct handling anymore since it\u0027s just an else clause in mergePropertySet now.",
      "parentUuid": "8f921509_bf01bf6e",
      "revId": "e5bf895264f4551430e9e33b4d738d80d75559ff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
